# Tracked files that a TOOL rewrites, not you.
#
# These land in the repo silently — stow and symlinks stay healthy, the change
# just sits uncommitted until you happen to run `git status` here. doctor.sh
# reports them, and shell/.config/shell/drift.sh nudges about them at terminal
# startup. Both read this file, so add a path once and both pick it up.
#
# One repo-relative path per line. Blank lines and #-comments are ignored.
# Paths must not contain spaces (drift.sh word-splits the list in POSIX sh).
#
# Deliberately NOT the whole repo: a warning that fires on every ordinary
# dotfiles edit is one you learn to ignore.

# Claude Code rewrites this on /config, /effort, plugin toggles, and accepted
# permission dialogs.
claude/.claude/settings.json
